  "result": "I implemented `slugify` in `src/strings.js` and added 11 tests to `test/strings.test.js`. `npm test` passes: 13 of 13, including the two existing `capitalize` tests.\n\nHow it works, in order:\n1. Lowercase the text.\n2. Split accented letters into a base letter plus accent marks, then drop the marks. This turns `ế` into `e` and `ñ` into `n`.\n3. Map Latin letters that step 2 can't split, using a small table: `đ`/`ð`→`d`, `ø`→`o`, `ł`→`l`, `ß`→`ss`, `æ`→`ae`, `œ`→`oe`, `þ`→`th`, `ı`→`i`. You asked for `đ`/`Đ`; I added the others so other Latin text also comes out as plain ASCII.\n4. Replace each run of characters other than `a-z`/`0-9` with one `-`, then remove leading and trailing hyphens.\n5. Cut to 50 characters and remove any hyphens left at the end.\n\nThe tests cover Vietnamese text, `đ`/`Đ`, other accented Latin text (French and Spanish), collapsing runs of symbols, trimming, digits, empty and symbol-only input, and the length limit: a cut at 50, a cut that would end on a hyphen, and a slug of exactly 50 characters.\n\nText in non-Latin scripts, such as Chinese or Cyrillic, has no ASCII form under these rules, so it's removed and can leave an empty slug.",
